A||N||7||killerb15||Help Me Please!!!||||5||
Z||000000||killerb15||11-14-2000||03:31 PM||||Dear Fiero Owners, or whoever.<BR>I'm 15 years old and very interested in purchacing a fiero. An '86 GT is advertized in the local paper, it says "runs excellent, little to certify. $1000 obo(Canadian)". I called the number but the owner was on vacation for a week, but he will call me on the 18-19 of November. I'd like to know if there is anything in particular i should ask about the car so that my first car is not a Lemon. Thanks in advance! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||11-14-2000||03:56 PM||||Check the kilometres, but since you live near me, CHECK FOR RUST.. If the frame is rusty.. Forget it. I bought one without really checking it over. Man, was that a mistake... If it's rusty, forget about it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-14-2000||05:39 PM||||Definatly rust is the most important thing to check for. Other things to check would be engine components. Drive the car and see how it runs, make sure there is no bad engine noise, things like that. I bought my 86 GT and didnt check for rust, didnt even know anything about the car. I found out it is pretty rusty, but an all around great car. I am going to rebuild it completly just becuase of rust. Always an option if you enjoy things like that. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I><p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||killerb15||11-14-2000||06:51 PM||||Thanks for the great advice "Johnnyk" and "Seanh", i'll be sure to check the frame for rusting, as well as listening for any odd noises coming from the engine. If anyone has any more helpfull info i still have 5 days before i check out the car, Thanks Again||||reg||14
Z||000004||ROB MAC||11-14-2000||07:05 PM||||Pull back the carpet inside the trunk at the top side or ends . When you see the gaping holes which is fairly likely , then offer him two-fifty. (thats two dollars and fifty cents)||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||11-14-2000||08:46 PM||||Just another thing to look for, as is for any car, that all the power options, radio and fan (heating/cooling) work properly.  Exterior lights, you know things like that.  Also, make sure than when you test drive it, the odometer works!  Had a friend that bought a car with 188210 miles on it, it still has the same amount!  Its all the little things that can sometimes add up and get ya!<P>One last thing, being a Fiero, very prone to having scratches on the exterior door glass.  If they arent deep enough to be seen easily, get a glare on the window and see if they are starting.  If so, you may have to replace the dew wipes.  (Fun!!!)<P>------------------<BR>"The fish who keeps on swimming is the first to chill upstream"||||reg||5
Z||000006||88formula||11-14-2000||09:33 PM||||Don't forget to check the AC and run the VIN number through one of those web-sites to check its history. If it was in a bad accident than forget about it no matter what the owner says. Once are car has been in an accident it is never the same again no matter who repaired it. I learned the hard way!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever2||11-14-2000||10:33 PM||||Get two.  <BR>They're small.<BR>||||reg||1
